{"id":"mahabharata-3-239","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":239,"title":"एकोनचत्वारिंशदधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 239 · The Danavas summon Duryodhana","summary":{"en":"Shakuni urges him to make peace with the Pandavas instead, but Duryodhana, dressed in bark and kusha grass, begins his fast and his brothers vow to share his fate. The Danavas of the underworld, fearing to lose their ally, summon a sorceress who brings him to them by night.","kn":"ಬದಲಿಗೆ ಪಾಂಡವರೊಂದಿಗೆ ಸಂಧಿ ಮಾಡೆಂದು ಶಕುನಿ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಆದರೆ ನಾರುಬಟ್ಟೆ ದರ್ಭೆ ಧರಿಸಿ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನು ಉಪವಾಸ ಆರಂಭಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಸಹೋದರರು ಅವನ ಗತಿಯೇ ತಮ್ಮದೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾರೆ. ತಮ್ಮ ಮಿತ್ರನನ್ನು ಕಳೆದುಕೊಳ್ಳುವ ಭಯದಿಂದ ಪಾತಾಳದ ದಾನವರು ಕೃತ್ಯೆಯನ್ನು ಕರೆದು ರಾತ್ರಿ ಅವನನ್ನು ತಮ್ಮಲ್ಲಿಗೆ ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"शकुनि उसे इसके बजाय पाण्डवों से सन्धि करने को कहता है, पर वल्कल और कुश धारण कर दुर्योधन अनशन आरम्भ करता है और उसके भाई उसकी गति में साथ देने की प्रतिज्ञा करते हैं। अपने सहयोगी को खोने के भय से पाताल के दानव एक कृत्या को बुलाते हैं, जो रात में उसे उनके पास ले आती है।","te":"దానికి బదులు పాండవులతో సంధి చేసుకోమని శకుని చెబుతాడు, కానీ నారబట్టలు, దర్భలు ధరించి దుర్యోధనుడు ఉపవాసం ప్రారంభిస్తాడు, సోదరులు అతని గతే తమదని ప్రతిజ్ఞ చేస్తారు. తమ మిత్రుని కోల్పోతామనే భయంతో పాతాళ దానవులు కృత్యను పిలిచి రాత్రి అతనిని తమ వద్దకు తెప్పిస్తారు.","ta":"அதற்குப் பதில் பாண்டவர்களுடன் சமாதானம் செய்யுமாறு ஶகுனி சொல்ல, மரவுரியும் தர்ப்பையும் அணிந்து துரியோதனன் உண்ணாநோன்பைத் தொடங்க, சகோதரர்கள் அவன் கதியே தம் கதி என்கிறார்கள். தம் நண்பனை இழப்போமோ என்று அஞ்சிய பாதாள அசுரர்கள் ஒரு க்ருத்யையை அழைத்து இரவில் அவனைத் தம்மிடம் கொண்டுவரச் செய்கிறார்கள்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവരോട് പകരം സന്ധി ചെയ്യാൻ ശകുനി ഉപദേശിക്കുന്നു; പക്ഷേ മരവുരിയും ദർഭപ്പുല്ലും ധരിച്ച് ദുര്യോധനൻ ഉപവാസം തുടങ്ങുന്നു, സഹോദരന്മാർ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ വിധി പങ്കിടുമെന്ന് പ്രതിജ്ഞ ചെയ്യുന്നു. സഖ്യകക്ഷിയെ നഷ്ടപ്പെടുമെന്ന് ഭയന്ന പാതാളത്തിലെ ദാനവന്മാർ ഒരു മായാവിനിയെ വിളിച്ചുവരുത്തുന്നു; അവൾ രാത്രിയിൽ ദുര്യോധനനെ അവരുടെ അടുത്തേക്ക് കൊണ്ടുപോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.239; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"घोषयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Ghoshayatra Parva (The cattle expedition)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"प्रायोपविष्टं राजानं दुर्योधनममर्षणम् ।\nउवाच सान्त्वयन्राजञ्शकुनिः सौबलस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shakuni, son of Subala, spoke consolingly to King Duryodhana, who sat fasting in his anger."}},{"n":2,"text":"सम्यगुक्तं हि कर्णेन तच्छ्रुतं कौरव त्वया ।\nमयाहृतां श्रियं स्फीतां मोहात्समपहाय किम् ।\nत्वमबुद्ध्या नृपवर प्राणानुत्स्रष्टुमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Karna has spoken rightly, and you have heard it, Kaurava. Why do you, in your folly, throw away the great prosperity I won for you and want to give up your life, O best of kings?"}},{"n":3,"text":"अद्य चाप्यवगच्छामि न वृद्धाः सेवितास्त्वया ।\nयः समुत्पतितं हर्षं दैन्यं वा न नियच्छति ।\nस नश्यति श्रियं प्राप्य पात्रमाममिवाम्भसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even now I see you have not waited on the elders. A man who cannot hold back sudden joy or despair loses his fortune once he has it, like an unbaked pot in water."}},{"n":4,"text":"अतिभीरुमतिक्लीबं दीर्घसूत्रं प्रमादिनम् ।\nव्यसनाद्विषयाक्रान्तं न भजन्ति नृपं श्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Prosperity does not attend a king who is too timid, too weak, slow to act, careless, or overcome by sensual pleasures in misfortune."}},{"n":5,"text":"सत्कृतस्य हि ते शोको विपरीते कथं भवेत् ।\nमा कृतं शोभनं पार्थैः शोकमालम्ब्य नाशय ॥","meaning":{"en":"You were honored, so how could grief come from the reverse? Do not take up sorrow and ruin the kindness the Pandavas did you."}},{"n":6,"text":"यत्र हर्षस्त्वया कार्यः सत्कर्तव्याश्च पाण्डवाः ।\nतत्र शोचसि राजेन्द्र विपरीतमिदं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where you should rejoice and honor the Pandavas, you grieve there, king of kings. Your attitude is the wrong way round."}},{"n":7,"text":"प्रसीद मा त्यजात्मानं तुष्टश्च सुकृतं स्मर ।\nप्रयच्छ राज्यं पार्थानां यशो धर्ममवाप्नुहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Be calm, do not abandon yourself; be content and remember the good done to you. Give the Pandavas their kingdom and gain fame and dharma."}},{"n":8,"text":"क्रियामेतां समाज्ञाय कृतघ्नो न भविष्यसि ।\nसौभ्रात्रं पाण्डवैः कृत्वा समवस्थाप्य चैव तान् ।\nपित्र्यं राज्यं प्रयच्छैषां ततः सुखमवाप्नुहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing this as the right course you will not be ungrateful. Make friendship with the Pandavas, establish them, return their ancestral kingdom, and then find happiness.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"शकुनेस्तु वचः श्रुत्वा दुःशासनमवेक्ष्य च ।\nपादयोः पतितं वीरं विक्लवं भ्रातृसौहृदात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Shakuni's words, and seeing the hero Duhshasana fallen at his feet, distraught out of love for his brother,"}},{"n":10,"text":"बाहुभ्यां साधुजाताभ्यां दुःशासनमरिंदमम् ।\nउत्थाप्य संपरिष्वज्य प्रीत्याजिघ्रत मूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana lifted that subduer of foes with his well-formed arms, embraced him and kissed him on the head with affection."}},{"n":11,"text":"कर्णसौबलयोश्चापि संस्मृत्य वचनान्यसौ ।\nनिर्वेदं परमं गत्वा राजा दुर्योधनस्तदा ।\nव्रीडयाभिपरीतात्मा नैराश्यमगमत्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Remembering also the words of Karna and Shakuni, King Duryodhana, filled with great dejection and overcome with shame, sank into utter despair."}},{"n":12,"text":"सुहृदां चैव तच्छ्रुत्वा समन्युरिदमब्रवीत् ।\nन धर्मधनसौख्येन नैश्वर्येण न चाज्ञया ।\nनैव भोगैश्च मे कार्यं मा विहन्यत गच्छत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his friends, he said in anger, \"I have no use for dharma, wealth, pleasure, rule, command or enjoyments. Do not stop me; go.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"निश्चितेयं मम मतिः स्थिता प्रायोपवेशने ।\nगच्छध्वं नगरं सर्वे पूज्याश्च गुरवो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"My mind is made up and fixed on fasting to death. All of you go to the city, and honor my elders.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"त एवमुक्ताः प्रत्यूचू राजानमरिमर्दनम् ।\nया गतिस्तव राजेन्द्र सास्माकमपि भारत ।\nकथं वा संप्रवेक्ष्यामस्त्वद्विहीनाः पुरं वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told this, they replied to the king, crusher of foes: \"Whatever your fate is, king of kings, it is ours too. How could we enter the city without you?\""}},{"n":15,"text":"स सुहृद्भिरमात्यैश्च भ्रातृभिः स्वजनेन च ।\nबहुप्रकारमप्युक्तो निश्चयान्न व्यचाल्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though his friends, ministers, brothers and kinsmen urged him in many ways, he did not shift from his resolve."}},{"n":16,"text":"दर्भप्रस्तरमास्तीर्य निश्चयाद्धृतराष्ट्रजः ।\nसंस्पृश्यापः शुचिर्भूत्वा भूतलं समुपाश्रितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Resolved, Dhritarashtra's son spread a mat of darbha grass, sipped water to purify himself and sat down on the ground."}},{"n":17,"text":"कुशचीराम्बरधरः परं नियममास्थितः ।\nवाग्यतो राजशार्दूलः स स्वर्गगतिकाङ्क्षया ।\nमनसोपचितिं कृत्वा निरस्य च बहिष्क्रियाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wearing kusha grass and bark garments, tiger among kings, he kept to a strict vow and silence, longing for the path to heaven, collecting his mind in worship and giving up outward activity."}},{"n":18,"text":"अथ तं निश्चयं तस्य बुद्ध्वा दैतेयदानवाः ।\nपातालवासिनो रौद्राः पूर्वं देवैर्विनिर्जिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Daityas and Danavas, who dwell in the nether world, fierce beings defeated earlier by the gods, learned of his resolve."}},{"n":19,"text":"ते स्वपक्षक्षयं तं तु ज्ञात्वा दुर्योधनस्य वै ।\nआह्वानाय तदा चक्रुः कर्म वैतानसंभवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing that his death would destroy their own side, they performed a rite based on the Vedic sacrificial ritual to summon Duryodhana."}},{"n":20,"text":"बृहस्पत्युशनोक्तैश्च मन्त्रैर्मन्त्रविशारदाः ।\nअथर्ववेदप्रोक्तैश्च याश्चोपनिषदि क्रियाः ।\nमन्त्रजप्यसमायुक्तास्तास्तदा समवर्तयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Expert in mantras, they performed rites taught in the mantras of Brihaspati and Ushanas, in the Atharva Veda and the Upanishads, with muttered mantras."}},{"n":21,"text":"जुह्वत्यग्नौ हविः क्षीरं मन्त्रवत्सुसमाहिताः ।\nब्राह्मणा वेदवेदाङ्गपारगाः सुदृढव्रताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins, masters of the Vedas and their limbs and firm in their vows, with full attention offered milk oblations into the fire with mantras."}},{"n":22,"text":"कर्मसिद्धौ तदा तत्र जृम्भमाणा महाद्भुता ।\nकृत्या समुत्थिता राजन्किं करोमीति चाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the rite succeeded, a great and marvelous being, a Kritya, rose up there, yawning, and said, \"What shall I do?\""}},{"n":23,"text":"आहुर्दैत्याश्च तां तत्र सुप्रीतेनान्तरात्मना ।\nप्रायोपविष्टं राजानं धार्तराष्ट्रमिहानय ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Daityas, with great delight in their hearts, said to her, \"Bring Dhritarashtra's son, the king, who sits fasting, here.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"तथेति च प्रतिश्रुत्य सा कृत्या प्रययौ तदा ।\nनिमेषादगमच्चापि यत्र राजा सुयोधनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So be it,\" she promised and went, and in an instant she reached the place where King Suyodhana was."}},{"n":25,"text":"समादाय च राजानं प्रविवेश रसातलम् ।\nदानवानां मुहूर्ताच्च तमानीतं न्यवेदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"She took the king and entered the underworld, and in a moment presented him to the Danavas."}},{"n":26,"text":"तमानीतं नृपं दृष्ट्वा रात्रौ संहत्य दानवाः ।\nप्रहृष्टमनसः सर्वे किंचिदुत्फुल्ललोचनाः ।\nसाभिमानमिदं वाक्यं दुर्योधनमथाब्रुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the king brought in the night, all the Danavas gathered with glad minds and eyes slightly wide with joy, and spoke these proud words to Duryodhana."}}]}]}